1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,029
Nearly 20 tons of cocaine.

2
00:00:03,029 --> 00:00:04,200
One cargo ship.

3
00:00:04,650 --> 00:00:05,777
June 17, 2019.

4
00:00:05,777 --> 00:00:09,480
Federal officers climb aboard a container ship

5
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:13,183
at the Packer Marine Terminal in Philadelphia.

6
00:00:13,633 --> 00:00:18,172
Inside seven of its containers, they find bricks.

7
00:00:18,172 --> 00:00:19,840
Thousands of them.

8
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:21,322
The final count:

9
00:00:21,322 --> 00:00:22,619
39,525 pounds.

10
00:00:22,619 --> 00:00:27,436
Customs puts the street value at about $1.3 billion.

11
00:00:27,886 --> 00:00:31,254
Customs calls it the largest cocaine seizure

12
00:00:31,254 --> 00:00:33,091
in its 230-year history.

13
00:00:33,541 --> 00:00:35,925
And it didn't come aboard in a port.

14
00:00:35,925 --> 00:00:38,972
According to prosecutors, it was lifted aboard

15
00:00:38,972 --> 00:00:41,753
at sea, at night, by the ship's own crane.

16
00:00:41,753 --> 00:00:42,879
So who loaded it?

17
00:00:42,879 --> 00:00:45,727
And how did 20 tons ride thousands of miles

18
00:00:45,727 --> 00:00:47,515
without anyone stopping it?

19
00:00:47,965 --> 00:00:50,781
This is the case of the MSC Gayane.

20
00:00:53,381 --> 00:00:54,575
Start with the ship.

21
00:00:55,025 --> 00:00:58,906
The MSC Gayane is a container ship, 1,030 feet

22
00:00:58,906 --> 00:01:02,280
long, sailing under the flag of Liberia.

23
00:01:02,280 --> 00:01:05,739
It was built in 2018, and operated by the

24
00:01:05,739 --> 00:01:09,788
Swiss-based Mediterranean Shipping Company, MSC.

25
00:01:10,238 --> 00:01:13,465
Ships like this carry thousands of steel boxes.

26
00:01:13,465 --> 00:01:16,623
Each container is closed with a numbered seal.

27
00:01:16,623 --> 00:01:20,056
If the seal is intact, the box hasn't been opened.

28
00:01:20,056 --> 00:01:23,145
That small piece of metal is the whole system

29
00:01:23,145 --> 00:01:23,763
of trust.

30
00:01:24,213 --> 00:01:27,250
In the spring of 2019, the Gayane leaves

31
00:01:27,250 --> 00:01:28,693
Europe on April 27.

32
00:01:28,693 --> 00:01:31,805
It crosses the Atlantic, goes through the

33
00:01:31,805 --> 00:01:34,766
Panama Canal, and turns south, down the

34
00:01:34,766 --> 00:01:37,120
Pacific coast of South America.

35
00:01:37,570 --> 00:01:39,801
After Chile, it turns north again:

36
00:01:39,801 --> 00:01:42,819
back through the canal, a stop in the Bahamas,

37
00:01:42,819 --> 00:01:44,263
and then Philadelphia.

38
00:01:44,263 --> 00:01:47,085
The next stop on the schedule is Rotterdam.

39
00:01:47,535 --> 00:01:49,511
On paper, an ordinary voyage.

40
00:01:49,511 --> 00:01:52,579
But somewhere off South America, the ship had

41
00:01:52,579 --> 00:01:53,124
company.

42
00:01:53,574 --> 00:01:54,534
The pickups.

43
00:01:54,984 --> 00:01:57,802
According to court records, speedboats came

44
00:01:57,802 --> 00:02:00,555
out to meet the Gayane at night, more than

45
00:02:00,555 --> 00:02:02,259
once, while it was at sea.

46
00:02:02,709 --> 00:02:05,463
A federal agent's affidavit says two crew

47
00:02:05,463 --> 00:02:08,553
members admitted loading cocaine from 14 boats

48
00:02:08,553 --> 00:02:09,023
at sea.

49
00:02:09,473 --> 00:02:10,939
The method was simple.

50
00:02:10,939 --> 00:02:13,871
The speedboats brought duffel bags of bricks

51
00:02:13,871 --> 00:02:14,804
in cargo nets.

52
00:02:14,804 --> 00:02:17,670
On the ship, a crane at the stern, normally

53
00:02:17,670 --> 00:02:20,735
used to lift supplies aboard, hoisted the nets

54
00:02:20,735 --> 00:02:21,868
up onto the deck.

55
00:02:22,318 --> 00:02:24,040
Then the crew went to work.

56
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:26,909
They hid the bags inside shipping containers,

57
00:02:26,909 --> 00:02:28,631
among the legitimate cargo.

58
00:02:28,631 --> 00:02:31,437
To fit it all in, prosecutors say, they bent

59
00:02:31,437 --> 00:02:34,051
railings and pulled back container doors.

60
00:02:34,501 --> 00:02:37,317
And then the trick that was supposed to make

61
00:02:37,317 --> 00:02:38,149
it invisible.

62
00:02:38,149 --> 00:02:40,901
Every container they opened got a new seal.

63
00:02:40,901 --> 00:02:43,781
A fake one, from a cache of counterfeit seals

64
00:02:43,781 --> 00:02:44,677
the gang kept.

65
00:02:45,127 --> 00:02:47,678
Investigators described one more move.

66
00:02:47,678 --> 00:02:50,632
On the way south, the first load went into a

67
00:02:50,632 --> 00:02:52,848
single container bound for Chile.

68
00:02:52,848 --> 00:02:55,667
That way, it would not be checked in Peru,

69
00:02:55,667 --> 00:02:58,621
where only the boxes coming off the ship got

70
00:02:58,621 --> 00:02:59,293
inspected.

71
00:02:59,743 --> 00:03:02,518
After Peru, the drugs were moved into the

72
00:03:02,518 --> 00:03:04,279
ship's ventilation system.

73
00:03:04,279 --> 00:03:07,460
After Chile, into containers headed for Europe.

74
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:10,304
More was loaded by crane on the run north,

75
00:03:10,304 --> 00:03:11,455
before the canal.

76
00:03:11,905 --> 00:03:14,718
The cocaine was never meant for Philadelphia.

77
00:03:14,718 --> 00:03:17,345
Investigators say it was bound for Europe.

78
00:03:17,795 --> 00:03:19,288
So who did the lifting?

79
00:03:19,738 --> 00:03:21,778
The Gayane had 22 crew members.

80
00:03:21,778 --> 00:03:24,739
Prosecutors would show that at least eight of

81
00:03:24,739 --> 00:03:25,989
them were in on it.

82
00:03:26,439 --> 00:03:29,408
Four were recruited before they ever boarded,

83
00:03:29,408 --> 00:03:32,114
by a criminal organization in Montenegro.

84
00:03:32,114 --> 00:03:35,083
One of them, the electrician, later said he'd

85
00:03:35,083 --> 00:03:38,053
been approached outside a café, by people who

86
00:03:38,053 --> 00:03:40,627
already knew about his upcoming voyage.

87
00:03:40,627 --> 00:03:43,398
He joined the ship in Antwerp, Belgium, in

88
00:03:43,398 --> 00:03:44,124
late April.

89
00:03:44,574 --> 00:03:47,739
The chief officer, Bosko Markovic, a seaman

90
00:03:47,739 --> 00:03:51,051
with 19 years at sea, managed the cargo plan.

91
00:03:51,051 --> 00:03:54,068
He knew which container would come off at

92
00:03:54,068 --> 00:03:54,878
which port.

93
00:03:55,328 --> 00:03:58,654
The engineer cadet, Nenad Ilic, ran the crane.

94
00:03:58,654 --> 00:04:01,979
And the electrician, Aleksandar Kavaja, passed

95
00:04:01,979 --> 00:04:05,088
information to the organizers on land, over

96
00:04:05,088 --> 00:04:08,414
so-called narco phones, about which containers

97
00:04:08,414 --> 00:04:09,643
were going where.

98
00:04:10,093 --> 00:04:12,899
After the ship left Europe, four more were

99
00:04:12,899 --> 00:04:13,634
brought in.

100
00:04:13,634 --> 00:04:14,837
A fourth engineer.

101
00:04:14,837 --> 00:04:16,374
An assistant reeferman.

102
00:04:16,374 --> 00:04:19,314
And two seamen from Samoa, who helped unload

103
00:04:19,314 --> 00:04:21,719
the bags and hide them in the cargo.

104
00:04:22,169 --> 00:04:25,170
One of those seamen told agents the second

105
00:04:25,170 --> 00:04:28,171
officer had recruited him, and that he was

106
00:04:28,171 --> 00:04:31,387
paid about €50,000 to help load cocaine on an

107
00:04:31,387 --> 00:04:32,459
earlier voyage.

108
00:04:32,459 --> 00:04:35,674
In his cabin, agents found a stack of 50-euro

109
00:04:35,674 --> 00:04:38,532
notes, hidden in a carton of cigarettes.

110
00:04:38,982 --> 00:04:40,090
An earlier voyage.

111
00:04:40,090 --> 00:04:42,922
Which means the June run may not have been the

112
00:04:42,922 --> 00:04:43,291
first.

113
00:04:43,741 --> 00:04:46,770
An investigator's affidavit places that

114
00:04:46,770 --> 00:04:48,868
earlier trip in the winter.

115
00:04:48,868 --> 00:04:52,440
That seaman had boarded in Antwerp on December

116
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:53,062
5, 2018.

117
00:04:53,062 --> 00:04:56,479
The second officer joined in Balboa, Panama,

118
00:04:56,479 --> 00:04:57,955
on January 4, 2019.

119
00:04:57,955 --> 00:05:01,528
The engineer cadet and the other Samoan seaman

120
00:05:01,528 --> 00:05:02,771
were aboard too.

121
00:05:03,221 --> 00:05:04,885
And then, the Delaware River.

122
00:05:05,335 --> 00:05:08,593
When the Gayane comes up the Delaware in June

123
00:05:08,593 --> 00:05:10,404
2019, a crowd is waiting:

124
00:05:10,404 --> 00:05:13,662
Homeland Security Investigations, Customs and

125
00:05:13,662 --> 00:05:16,632
Border Protection, the Coast Guard, state

126
00:05:16,632 --> 00:05:19,673
police from Pennsylvania and Delaware, and

127
00:05:19,673 --> 00:05:21,121
Philadelphia police.

128
00:05:21,571 --> 00:05:24,550
Court records don't say whether someone tipped

129
00:05:24,550 --> 00:05:25,132
them off.

130
00:05:25,132 --> 00:05:28,111
But one crew member, the engineer cadet, later

131
00:05:28,111 --> 00:05:30,765
admitted that when he saw law enforcement

132
00:05:30,765 --> 00:05:33,485
coming in Delaware Bay, he threw his narco

133
00:05:33,485 --> 00:05:34,521
phone overboard.

134
00:05:34,971 --> 00:05:37,621
On the night of June 16, officers spot

135
00:05:37,621 --> 00:05:40,132
something wrong in seven containers.

136
00:05:40,132 --> 00:05:43,340
The next day they confirm it, with fiber optic

137
00:05:43,340 --> 00:05:46,619
scopes, drug-sniffing dogs, and an X-ray truck.

138
00:05:47,069 --> 00:05:48,573
Seven containers.

139
00:05:48,573 --> 00:05:52,821
Inside each one, between 1,200 and 3,000 bricks.

140
00:05:52,821 --> 00:05:56,626
Early counts put the total at about 15,000.

141
00:05:57,076 --> 00:05:58,596
Then comes the counting.

142
00:05:58,596 --> 00:06:01,446
Officers pack the bricks into evidence boxes,

143
00:06:01,446 --> 00:06:03,092
and weigh them on a scale.

144
00:06:03,542 --> 00:06:07,457
The first estimate is about 16.5 tons.

145
00:06:07,457 --> 00:06:10,032
The number keeps growing.

146
00:06:10,032 --> 00:06:13,534
By June 26, the final count is in:

147
00:06:13,534 --> 00:06:14,977
39,525 pounds.

148
00:06:15,427 --> 00:06:18,381
At a news conference on June 21, officials

149
00:06:18,381 --> 00:06:20,562
stand behind a table of bricks.

150
00:06:20,562 --> 00:06:23,235
It's only about a quarter of the load.

151
00:06:23,685 --> 00:06:26,837
Within days, a federal complaint had charged

152
00:06:26,837 --> 00:06:29,917
the second officer and another crewman with

153
00:06:29,917 --> 00:06:30,705
conspiracy.

154
00:06:30,705 --> 00:06:33,284
Both, investigators said, confessed.

155
00:06:33,284 --> 00:06:36,293
By June 21, six crew members were charged.

156
00:06:36,743 --> 00:06:39,541
Casey Durst, Customs' director of field

157
00:06:39,541 --> 00:06:42,412
operations in Baltimore, gave the room a

158
00:06:42,412 --> 00:06:43,918
picture of the scale.

159
00:06:43,918 --> 00:06:47,004
Laid end to end, she said, the bricks would

160
00:06:47,004 --> 00:06:48,583
cover about 2.5 miles.

161
00:06:49,033 --> 00:06:51,507
Then the government went after the ship itself.

162
00:06:51,957 --> 00:06:55,370
On July 4, 2019, Customs executes a federal

163
00:06:55,370 --> 00:06:58,387
seizure warrant, and takes the Gayane.

164
00:06:58,387 --> 00:07:01,800
Durst calls it the largest vessel seized in

165
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:04,181
the agency's 230-year history.

166
00:07:04,181 --> 00:07:07,436
Seizing a ship this size, she said, is an

167
00:07:07,436 --> 00:07:09,579
unusual enforcement action.

168
00:07:10,029 --> 00:07:13,165
In the statement announcing the seizure, the U.S.

169
00:07:13,165 --> 00:07:16,109
Attorney in Philadelphia, William McSwain, put

170
00:07:16,109 --> 00:07:17,837
the whole case in one line.

171
00:07:18,287 --> 00:07:20,998
We found nearly 20 tons of cocaine hidden on

172
00:07:20,998 --> 00:07:21,615
this ship.

173
00:07:22,415 --> 00:07:24,921
It doesn't stay seized for long.

174
00:07:24,921 --> 00:07:28,054
The ship's owner and operator put up $10

175
00:07:28,054 --> 00:07:31,658
million in cash and a $40 million surety bond.

176
00:07:31,658 --> 00:07:33,146
$50 million in all.

177
00:07:33,146 --> 00:07:36,201
By mid-July, the Gayane is back at sea,

178
00:07:36,201 --> 00:07:37,924
heading for Rotterdam.

179
00:07:38,374 --> 00:07:41,029
Prosecutors have not accused MSC of any

180
00:07:41,029 --> 00:07:44,025
wrongdoing, and the company was not charged.

181
00:07:44,025 --> 00:07:47,021
It said that shipping firms are, quote, from

182
00:07:47,021 --> 00:07:50,153
time to time affected by trafficking problems,

183
00:07:50,153 --> 00:07:52,945
and that it took the case very seriously.

184
00:07:53,395 --> 00:07:57,222
But the Gayane wasn't the only problem that year.

185
00:07:57,222 --> 00:08:00,346
In March, at the same port, officers had

186
00:08:00,346 --> 00:08:03,548
pulled about 1,200 pounds of cocaine from

187
00:08:03,548 --> 00:08:06,984
containers on another MSC ship, the Desiree.

188
00:08:07,434 --> 00:08:10,900
In New Jersey, early that year, 3,200 pounds

189
00:08:10,900 --> 00:08:14,444
had turned up in a container that held mostly

190
00:08:14,444 --> 00:08:15,390
dried fruit.

191
00:08:15,390 --> 00:08:18,856
And in May, separately, about 450 kilos were

192
00:08:18,856 --> 00:08:20,746
seized at the same port.

193
00:08:21,196 --> 00:08:24,135
Customs suspended the line's status in its

194
00:08:24,135 --> 00:08:27,354
trusted-shipper program, C-TPAT, after the two

195
00:08:27,354 --> 00:08:28,684
Philadelphia cases.

196
00:08:29,134 --> 00:08:30,222
And the crew?

197
00:08:30,672 --> 00:08:33,594
All eight pleaded guilty to conspiracy to

198
00:08:33,594 --> 00:08:36,587
possess cocaine with intent to distribute,

199
00:08:36,587 --> 00:08:39,794
aboard a vessel subject to U.S. jurisdiction.

200
00:08:39,794 --> 00:08:42,431
In federal court in Philadelphia, the

201
00:08:42,431 --> 00:08:44,640
sentences came down one by one.

202
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:47,205
The last, at the end of August 2021.

203
00:08:47,655 --> 00:08:50,455
The chief officer and the engineer cadet:

204
00:08:50,455 --> 00:08:51,616
seven years each.

205
00:08:51,616 --> 00:08:52,913
The second officer:

206
00:08:52,913 --> 00:08:54,347
six and a half years.

207
00:08:54,347 --> 00:08:55,440
The electrician:

208
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:57,352
seven years and four months.

209
00:08:57,352 --> 00:08:58,717
The fourth engineer:

210
00:08:58,717 --> 00:09:00,493
five years and ten months.

211
00:09:00,493 --> 00:09:03,224
The reeferman and the two Samoan seamen:

212
00:09:03,224 --> 00:09:04,317
five years each.

213
00:09:04,767 --> 00:09:06,600
The captain was not charged.

214
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:09,152
Prosecutors said there was insufficient

215
00:09:09,152 --> 00:09:12,425
evidence to charge him, or any other crew members.

216
00:09:12,875 --> 00:09:15,498
Back in July 2019, Homeland Security

217
00:09:15,498 --> 00:09:17,830
Investigations had set its goal.

218
00:09:17,830 --> 00:09:21,036
Its special agent in charge in Philadelphia,

219
00:09:21,036 --> 00:09:24,024
Marlon Miller, said it wanted to bring to

220
00:09:24,024 --> 00:09:27,157
justice, quote, those who had roles in this

221
00:09:27,157 --> 00:09:28,833
drug smuggling venture.

222
00:09:29,633 --> 00:09:32,770
When the second officer and the engineer cadet

223
00:09:32,770 --> 00:09:35,976
were sentenced, in August 2021, the acting U.S.

224
00:09:35,976 --> 00:09:39,318
Attorney, Jennifer Arbittier Williams, said this.

225
00:09:39,768 --> 00:09:42,609
Drug smuggling operations will be uncovered

226
00:09:42,609 --> 00:09:43,864
one way or another.

227
00:09:44,664 --> 00:09:47,038
The crew was only one end of it.

228
00:09:47,038 --> 00:09:49,932
In October 2022, federal prosecutors in

229
00:09:49,932 --> 00:09:52,826
Brooklyn charged a man from Montenegro:

230
00:09:52,826 --> 00:09:55,794
Goran Gogic, a former heavyweight boxer.

231
00:09:55,794 --> 00:09:58,985
They allege he helped move cocaine on three

232
00:09:58,985 --> 00:10:02,176
MSC ships between 2018 and 2019, the Gayane

233
00:10:02,176 --> 00:10:02,992
among them.

234
00:10:02,992 --> 00:10:06,851
He has pleaded not guilty, and is presumed innocent.

235
00:10:07,301 --> 00:10:10,497
His trial was set to begin in November 2025.

236
00:10:10,497 --> 00:10:13,112
It never reached opening statements.

237
00:10:13,112 --> 00:10:16,309
The whole jury was dismissed after a plot to

238
00:10:16,309 --> 00:10:17,326
bribe a juror.

239
00:10:17,326 --> 00:10:20,086
Three men have since pleaded guilty to

240
00:10:20,086 --> 00:10:22,701
obstruction of justice in that plot.

241
00:10:22,701 --> 00:10:25,825
As of September 2026, no new trial date had

242
00:10:25,825 --> 00:10:26,842
been reported.

243
00:10:27,292 --> 00:10:29,971
Look at what actually broke in this case.

244
00:10:29,971 --> 00:10:30,821
Not a border.

245
00:10:30,821 --> 00:10:31,735
Not a scanner.

246
00:10:31,735 --> 00:10:34,414
A container seal is a promise that nobody

247
00:10:34,414 --> 00:10:35,395
opened the box.

248
00:10:35,395 --> 00:10:38,008
On the Gayane, the people who broke that

249
00:10:38,008 --> 00:10:39,446
promise were the crew.

250
00:10:39,446 --> 00:10:41,929
And the only reason we know is that in

251
00:10:41,929 --> 00:10:43,889
Philadelphia, someone checked.

252
00:10:44,339 --> 00:10:46,869
So here's what the record shows.

253
00:10:46,869 --> 00:10:49,004
14 boats at sea. One crane.

254
00:10:49,004 --> 00:10:52,088
Seven containers with suspicious seals.

255
00:10:52,088 --> 00:10:54,064
39,525 pounds of cocaine.

256
00:10:54,064 --> 00:10:57,385
Eight sailors sentenced to federal prison.

257
00:10:57,385 --> 00:11:01,180
And one question the crew's case never answered:

258
00:11:01,180 --> 00:11:05,054
had it worked before Philadelphia, and how often?

259
00:11:05,504 --> 00:11:06,641
Case file 012.

260
00:11:06,641 --> 00:11:08,753
The crew's case is closed.

261
00:11:08,753 --> 00:11:12,245
The alleged organizer's case is still open.
